       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. The usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nSome possible next steps:\n- **Was this a typo?** If you meant 10 mg once daily, or a lower starting dose such as 5 mg, I can enter that right away.\n- **Is the patient already on 10 mg and still uncontrolled?** Adding a second agent from a different class is usually preferred over going above the maximum. Options include an ACE inhibitor or ARB, a thiazide-like diuretic, or a beta-blocker, depending on the indication.\n- **Is there an unusual reason for 20 mg?** If so, please check it with your resident or attending and pharmacy. Once it's confirmed, tell me and I can enter it with a note documenting the approval.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
     ],
